  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nSW flow aloft will be over Montana today as the upper ridge moves\neast and upper trough/low moves inland from the Pacific. \n\nThe SW flow aloft will bring increasing moisture and instability\ninto NE Montana today with chances for showers and thunderstorms\ndeveloping across the region. The chances for showers and\nthunderstorms will continue at times tonight. \n\nThe upper low moves into Montana Sunday morning> A cold front will\nmove through eastern Montana during the day on Sunday with showers\nand thunderstorms at times. West winds behind the cold front\nSunday afternoon may be strong enough for a Lake Wind Advisory\nover Fort Peck Lake. SPC has a Marginal Risk over most of the\nforecast area for severe weather on Sunday with damaging winds\nbeing the main threat. \n\nThe upper low moves into Alberta and Saskatchewan Sunday night\nwith most of Montana moving into a dry slot. The upper low will be\nover Saskatchewan on Monday with the dry slot and gusty west winds\nover the forecast area. A Lake Wind Advisory is likely for Fort\nPeck Lake on Monday. \n\nHigh pressure moves into the area Monday night with diminishing\nwinds and upper ridge will bring dry weather with warmer\ntemperatures on Tuesday. \n\nSW flow aloft is expected Wednesday and beyond with an upper\ntrough/low over the Pacific NW and and upper ridge to the east. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nOnly deviation to NBM was to tweak PoPs today through Sunday.\n\nThere is high confidence that there will be showers and\nthunderstorms at times this afternoon, tonight and Sunday with low\nconfidence in timing and precipitation amounts.",
